From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:08:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/52] backends: let the shell treat held modifiers as used up

Add clutter_seat_consume_held_modifiers(). A shortcut made of modifiers
alone, such as one held to dictate, can call it once it takes effect:
the modifiers held at that moment stop counting until their keys are
pressed again, so pointer, touchpad and keyboard input, the key symbols
it produces and the keyboard state clients see behave as if they weren't
held. The native seat clears them from its xkb state and queues a key
state event, which now also sends the new modifiers to Wayland clients.
---
